# Personalise your home

Your Home Assistant interface belongs to your household or business. Use a name people recognise, with a family crest, household emblem or business logo if it helps them recognise the space. A clear text name is enough.

civica identifies the theme project, its documentation and promotion. It is not a required name or logo inside your home. The [project identity guide](../styles/brand.html) applies when referring to the project itself.

## What you can do now

Home Assistant supports named dashboards and picture cards. These are existing native features; this page does not change your installation.

1. Choose a recognisable dashboard title, such as “Morgan household” or “Example workshop”. Keep built-in page names where Home Assistant owns them. A dashboard title does not rename accounts, entities or devices.
2. If an image helps, add a native Picture card and use its **Upload picture** option or an existing authorised image. Keep the name available as text and provide suitable alternative text.
3. Set the picture's action deliberately. An identity image should not unexpectedly turn on a device. A home link should lead to the actual dashboard home; an image that has no action should not look like a button.
4. Check the result on a phone, with keyboard navigation and enlarged text. Keep the room names, current states and essential actions more prominent than decorative artwork.

The official [dashboard guidance](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/dashboards/) describes dashboard titles and configuration. The [Picture card guidance](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/picture/) documents image upload, alternative text and actions. Review these against the version you use before changing a setup.

## Proposed theme personalisation

The following headers define the design-system target for optional shell personalisation. They are reference examples, not new theme settings. The current companion still inserts civica artwork into supported sidebar and browser identity surfaces; a global family-name, crest or logo setting has not been implemented. See the [compatibility record](compatibility.html#household-identity-transition).

| Choice | Required behaviour |
| --- | --- |
| No custom identity | Retain the native title or chosen dashboard name. Do not insert a project logo automatically. |
| Text name | Display the exact household or business name and allow it to wrap. Do not change account or device names. |
| Optional crest or logo | Preserve its proportions and colours, with a readable name alongside it. A logo is not a requirement. |
| Remove the image | Return to the text name without losing navigation or changing the selected palette. |
| Image fails to load | Keep the text name and all navigation usable. |

